  "limits": [
    "Coverage is for the currently registered unified MAC rule catalogue; adding arbitrary crypto/native labels needs new classification proofs.",
    "The case numbers count parameterized typed forms, not concrete instances, internal pure-wire critical pairs or global finite-basis size.",
    "Fusion completeness applies with fusion at the root of the whole source. Context lifting handles both edits inside one shared hole, not arbitrary competitors overlapping the outer placement.",
    "Old/new pure-wire proof comparison, wire-internal root/fixed-structure overlaps, association, crypto-tail and wire-tail resolution remain incomplete.",
    "The unified rewrite system remains nonterminating under unrestricted expansion; no global convergence or higher-basis completeness follows.",
    "Higher constructor counts exclude wiring/context/boundary payload, libraries, dependencies and generation/checking cost. No ordinary shared-proof advantage established.",
    "Stateful repair is endpoint kernel equality within the updated checked model. It does not establish across-revision equality or compare extracted compilers, runtime or quantitative losses.",
    "Full mixed code-changing reduction/native/cryptographic error integration and internal oracle runtime remain outstanding."
  ],
